Given the sequence $\{a_n\}$ with the general term formula $a_n = 2^n - (-1)^n$, where $n \in \mathbb{N}^*$. Let $a_{n_1}, a_{n_2}, \ldots, a_{n_t}$ (where $n_1 < n_2 < \ldots < n_t$, $t \in \mathbb{N}^*$) form an arithmetic sequence.
(1) If $t=3$.
   ① When $n_1, n_2, n_3$ are consecutive positive integers, find the value of $n_1$;
   ② When $n_1 = 1$, prove that $n_3 - n_2$ is a constant value;
(2) Find the maximum value of $t$.

s:
(1) ① According to the problem, $a_{n_1}, a_{n_1+1}, a_{n_1+2}$ form an arithmetic sequence, which means $2a_{n_1+1} = a_{n_1} + a_{n_1+2}$,
thus $2[2^{n_1+1} - (-1)^{n_1+1}] = 2^{n_1} - (-1)^{n_1} + 2^{n_1+2} - (-1)^{n_1+2}$,
when $n_1$ is odd, solving gives $2^{n_1} = -4$, which is impossible for any positive integer $n_1$;
when $n_1$ is even, solving gives $2^{n_1} = 4$, so $n_1 = 2$. (3 points)
② According to the problem, $a_1, a_{n_2}, a_{n_3}$ form an arithmetic sequence, which means $2a_{n_2} = a_1 + a_{n_3}$,
thus $2[2^{n_2} - (-1)^{n_2}] = 3 + 2^{n_3} - (-1)^{n_3}$,
when both $n_2$ and $n_3$ are odd, $2^{n_2} - 2^{n_3-1} = 1$, the left side is even, which is a contradiction;
when both $n_2$ and $n_3$ are even, $2^{n_2-1} - 2^{n_3-2} = 1$, the left side is even, which is a contradiction;
when $n_2$ is even and $n_3$ is odd, $2^{n_2+1} - 2^{n_3} = 5$, the left side is even, which is a contradiction;
when $n_2$ is odd and $n_3$ is even, $2^{n_2+1} - 2^{n_3} = 0$, which means $n_3 - n_2 = 1$. (8 points)
(2) Suppose $a_s, a_r, a_t$ ($s < r < t$) form an arithmetic sequence, then $2a_r = a_s + a_t$,
which means $2[2^r - (-1)^r] = 2^s - (-1)^s + 2^t - (-1)^t$,
after rearranging, $2^s + 2^t - 2^{r+1} = (-1)^s + (-1)^t - 2(-1)^r$,
if $t = r+1$, then $2^s = (-1)^s - 3(-1)^r$, since $2^s \geq 2$, $(-1)^s - 3(-1)^r$ can only be 2 or 4,
thus $s$ can only be 1 or 2; (12 points)
if $t \geq r+2$, then $2^s + 2^t - 2^{r+1} \geq 2^s + 2^{r+2} - 2^{r+1} \geq 2 + 2^4 - 2^3 = 10$, $(-1)^s + (-1)^t - 2(-1)^r \leq 4$,
which is a contradiction,
in conclusion, only $a_1, a_r, a_{r+1}$ or $a_2, a_r, a_{r+1}$ can form an arithmetic sequence, where $r$ is odd,
thus the maximum value of $t$ is $\boxed{3}$. (16 points)

